{
  "uid": "course-51daa6433b016ba1031d2c61",
  "title": "Lab 36: Model KV retention and restore decisions",
  "tags": [
    "gpu-course",
    "llm-inference",
    "36_kv_tiering"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 3,
  "editable": false,
  "timezone": "utc",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "description": "Does TTL expire before the next reuse even when capacity is ample? Does increasing storage capacity help a low-reuse workload? Can a storage hit be rejected as too costly? After a modeled restart, only prefixes previously demoted to storage survive; exclusive tiers are not a persistent backup of every device entry. Explain why changing identity prevents reuse while a mere capacity change does not. This CPU retention model simulates cache placement without transferring GPU data or running inference. Missing metrics remain unknown; sampled telemetry is context, not a timing measurement. Nsight Systems: This CPU retention model simulates cache placement without transferring GPU data or running inference.",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "workspace",
        "type": "textbox",
        "label": "Fixed learner workspace",
        "current": {
          "text": "learner-01",
          "value": "learner-01"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "profile",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "small,large",
        "current": {
          "text": "small",
          "value": "small"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "node",
        "type": "query",
        "label": "Node exporter instance",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "course-soperator-metrics"
        },
        "query": "label_values(node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes, instance)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "refresh": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Selected comparison generation",
      "type": "table",
      "description": "These are explicitly selected completed runs. Submission of another job does not replace them. Summary panels always show the current selected pair, even with a historical time range. Check generation and experiment timestamps.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "course-soperator-metrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(course_lab_publication_generation{course=\"llm-inference\",lab=\"36_kv_tiering\",workspace=\"$workspace\",profile=\"$profile\"} @ now())",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "format": "table",
          "legendFormat": "{{Hostname}} GPU {{gpu}}",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "noValue": "No measured data"
        },
